@startuml seq-12-password-reset-otp
title Password Reset — OTP Self-Service Flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
autonumber

actor "User\n(Angular)" as User
participant "Gateway\n:9000" as GW
participant "Auth Service\n:9001" as Auth
participant "OtpService\n(in-memory\n10 min TTL)" as OTP
participant "ResetToken\nService\n(in-memory\n10 min)" as RT
participant "Keycloak\n:8081" as KC
participant "Mail Service\n(Gmail SMTP)" as Mail

== Step 1: Request OTP ==

User -> GW : POST /api/auth/forgot-password\n{ email: "analyst@example.com" } (Public)
GW -> Auth : route (permitAll)
Auth -> KC : Admin API GET /users?email=analyst@example.com
KC --> Auth : user found { id, username, email }
Auth -> OTP : generate 6-digit OTP for email\n10 min TTL, ≤5 attempts
OTP --> Auth : OTP code
Auth -> Mail : sendOtp(email, otp)\n(Gmail SMTP via spring-boot-starter-mail)
Auth --> User : 200 { message:"OTP sent if account exists" }
note right of Auth : No enumeration — same response\nwhether email exists or not

== Step 2: Verify OTP ==

User -> GW : POST /api/auth/verify-otp\n{ email, otp:"482917" } (Public)
GW -> Auth : route
Auth -> OTP : verify(email, otp)
alt OTP correct + not expired
  OTP --> Auth : valid
  Auth -> RT : issue single-use resetToken\n(UUID, 10 min TTL)
  RT --> Auth : resetToken
  Auth --> User : 200 { resetToken }
else OTP wrong or expired
  Auth --> User : 400 { error:"Invalid or expired OTP" }
end

== Step 3: Set New Password ==

User -> GW : POST /api/auth/reset-password\n{ resetToken, newPassword } (Public)
GW -> Auth : route
Auth -> RT : consume(resetToken) → email
Auth -> KC : Admin API GET /users?email=…
KC --> Auth : { id }
Auth -> KC : Admin API PUT /users/{id}/reset-password\n{ type:"password", temporary:false,\n  value:newPassword }
KC --> Auth : 204 password updated

Auth --> User : 200 { message:"Password updated" }
User -> User : redirect to /login

@enduml
